   (from `assets/app-template.index.html`, comments stripped) and `js/app.js` (vanilla, no preprocessors).
 - Step-def authors: the `the app is reloaded` step must preserve the current `location.hash` across
   the happy-dom window rebuild, or the routing-persistence scenario cannot hold its state.
+
+## Voyage: DOM identity on state change (browser-only defect)
+
+- Acceptance (Cypress, real browser) fails because `render()` rebuilds `.todo-list` via
+  `innerHTML = ''`, detaching the list-item nodes a client holds before a click. happy-dom also
+  detaches on `innerHTML = ''`, so the in-suite cucumber tier CAN reproduce it.
+- `features/complete.feature` and `features/edit.feature` now pin element-identity preservation:
+  five scenarios capture a list-item node, perform the state change, and assert the same node is
+  still attached. They redden on the current `render()`-rebuild code and green only when the app
+  mutates the existing node in place (toggle class/checkbox, update mark-all, cancel edit in place).
+- `watchbill.json` `watch1` lists the five scenarios as the QM target set. QM must add the two new
+  step patterns (`the list item for {string} is captured`, `the list item for {string} is the
+  captured node`); until then they are undefined and the scenarios fail as intended.
+- Crew fix lives in `js/app.js` seams (`toggle`, `toggleAll`, the Escape branch in `init`): mutate
+  the live node instead of calling `render()` for these interactions. No production code written here.
diff --git a/features/complete.feature b/features/complete.feature
index bb5e963..195059a 100644
--- a/features/complete.feature
+++ b/features/complete.feature
@@ -44,3 +44,44 @@ Feature: Completing and toggling todos
     When the user checks the mark all as complete checkbox
     And the user clicks clear completed
     Then the mark all as complete checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Rule: State changes preserve list item element identity
+    The app MUST mutate each existing list item node in place (toggle its
+    completed class and checkbox, or update the mark-all checkbox) instead of
+    rebuilding the list. An element a client holds before the change stays
+    attached to the DOM across the interaction, so references taken before the
+    click remain valid afterwards.
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo keeps its list item element attached
+    Given the app has the active todo "feed the cat"
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is captured
+    When the user checks the todo "feed the cat"
+    Then the todo "feed the cat" is marked completed
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is the captured node
+
+  Scenario: Un-completing a todo keeps its list item element attached
+    Given the app has the completed todo "feed the cat"
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is captured
+    When the user unchecks the todo "feed the cat"
+    Then the todo "feed the cat" is not marked completed
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is the captured node
+
+  Scenario: Marking all complete keeps every list item element attached
+    Given the app has the active todo "feed the cat"
+    And the app has the active todo "walk the dog"
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is captured
+    And the list item for "walk the dog" is captured
+    When the user checks the mark all as complete checkbox
+    Then every todo is marked completed
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is the captured node
+    And the list item for "walk the dog" is the captured node
+
+  Scenario: Clearing all complete keeps every list item element attached
+    Given the app has the completed todo "feed the cat"
+    And the app has the completed todo "walk the dog"
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is captured
+    And the list item for "walk the dog" is captured
+    When the user unchecks the mark all as complete checkbox
+    Then every todo is not marked completed
+    And the list item for "feed the cat" is the captured node
+    And the list item for "walk the dog" is the captured node
